{title: Let the Lower Lights Be Burning}
{artist: Philip Bliss}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 88}

Verse 1
[F]Brightly beams our [Bb]Father's [F]mercy from his lighthouse [C]evermore,
[F]but to us he [Bb]gives the [F]keeping of the [C]lights along the [F]shore.

Chorus
[F]Let the lower [Bb]lights be [F]burning! Send a gleam across the [C]wave!
[F]Some poor fainting, [Bb]struggling [F]seaman [C]you may rescue, [F]you may save.
